  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n of the Kephalaia Chapter\n\n\n---\n\n\n**\n¶2:**\n What\n the in\nmost nature\n of the\n Divine\n is\n in\n itself —\n no understanding\n can re\ncount or dis\nclose how\n it exists from\n eternity —\n all things\n within\n it\n remain\n ve\niled in\n the\n infinite\n itself\n. The beginning\n of et\nernity and its\n end cannot\n be comprehended,\n for the\n Divine exce\neds every\n capacity\n of thought to\n set\n it\n within\n limits\n.\n\n**¶3:** Now\n, the\n realm\n of spiritual death — that\n is, the state of evil and fals\nity in\n their\n own\n nature —\n and\n the essence\n of\n the Divine\n which\n exists forever and\n ever:\n these\n two\n stand\n over\n against one another.\n\n**¶\n4:** As\n for the eternity of evil and fals\nity,\n which\n exist\n from\n the\n most\n ancient state\n, no understanding\n is\n able\n to comprehend how they\n subs\nist in themselves. For no other power\n is manifest\n within\n them by\n which their\n origin might be spoken\n of\n or\n recounted. However, from the time\n when evil stirred itself and rose up\n against wisdom, desiring to come\n and\n dom\ninate the state of spiritual life, its\n nature could\n begin\n to be known\n by\n contrast\n.\n\n\n**¶5:** Divine\n Truth in its first proceeding came\n forth against\n evil and prevented it;\n He\n kept it apart from the interior\n mind\n where\n spiritual\n life dw\nells. He\n held\n it back. From that time, when\n wisdom was inter\nmin\ngled with falsity, and spiritual life\n with spiritual death, there came\n a capacity\n and\n a\n permission for the celest\nial truths and for\n those\n who are\n sent\n to teach,\n to speak\n and\n dis\nclose how the prof\nan\nation and the spiritual\n combat came\n to\n pass —\n how wisdom became entangled with fals\nity,\n and how\n life\n became\n bound\n within\n the\n midst\n of death.\n\n**¶6\n:** After evil stirred itself\n in its own nature, its intention\n spread through its\n own\n realm.\n It\n filled\n the entire state\n of falsity with itself\n,\n perce\niving the rad\niance of wisdom in\n the\n depth\n below\n it\n. For\n the\n nature of evil\n within\n itself —\n because\n its\n prop\nrium r\neckoned itself mighty\n — this\n first hered\nitary nature made\n its\n will\n obst\ninate and its\n resistance\n harder\n than any created\n substance\n,\n sur\npassing all things\n as\n they\n exist in the natural\n world.\n\n**¶7:**\n The\n state\n of spiritual death and\n the\n en\nvy that\n belongs\n to evil,\n which perv\nades the whole\n realm of falsity —\n its\n deliber\nate mal\nice and wick\nedness infl\nicted\n injuries\n against\n the realm\n of spiritual\n life.\n\n**¶8:**\n Then\n the\n Divine\n proce\neding moved\n toward\n the\n realm\n of fals\nity.\n Evil\n drew the\n powers of the Divine into\n itself;\n the\n ent\nang\nlement was\n deep\n,\n and\n the Divine\n became\n hidden\n within those\n states\n.\n\n**¶9:** Evil\n spread itself out.\n It generated from\n itself five fundamental states of falsity and\n perv\nerted\n love\n: obscurity of thought,\n self-love, vain reasoning,\n falsified\n truth\n, and \nutter spiritual\n ignorance. From\n these there\n sprouted false perceptions.\n Evil\n rose\n up and\n formed itself according\n to its own nature;\n it generated from\n itself through\n successive\n deriv\nations inn\numerable states\n, none\n resemb\nling another\n.\n In the memories of its lowest\n prop\nrium, it produced\n many destruct\nive aff\nections —\n d\nevouring reason\nings, and\n fierce lusts for\n domin\nion.\n These were established and\n grew powerful\n in the hideous forms that\n belong\n to spiritual\n darkness\n, and by their fury\n,\n by their wick\nedness and\n mutual\n hatred, they destroyed one another even\n as they war\nred among themselves.\n\n**¶\n10:** Then\n the deliber\nation\n of the ruling self-love subd\nued its own realm and its own\n powers beneath\n itself\n. It perceived the nature of wisdom from\n af\nar.\n It conspired to wage spiritual\n war against the heavenly kingdom and\n the Divine order\n that gov\nerns it.\n\n**¶11\n:** However\n, the Divine Itself, the Father\n of all\n Good\n, also\n knew of this\n war, this\n intention\n to\n overthrow the\n state\n of wisdom\n. In the\n providence\n of His\n infinite\n fore\nknowledge, He transformed Himself —\n He\n turned\n His\n proce\neding forth\n to\n meet evil\n and\n oppose\n it.\n\n**¶12:**\n Indeed\n, at that time the\n conflict\n was\n ordained\n to\n come forth\n against\n the Divine.\n \n*(\nThe\n fragment\n res\nists\n full\n translation;\n the spiritual\n sense is\n that\n the\n crisis\n of opposition\n to\n the\n Divine reached\n its appointed\n moment.)*\n\n**¶13\n:** Evil poured itself out into its\n fundamental states:\n into\n obscurity of\n thought, into self-love, into\n vain reasoning, into falsified truth\n, and\n into complete spiritual\n ignorance. It rose from the deep\nest proprium, establishing itself within\n false perceptions and\n marsh\naling them\n against\n wisdom.\n\n**¶14:**\n Also\n, at the time when evil generated itself\n and formed its works —\n its\n fruits — it remained\n ro\noted within\n them. Then\n there\n were summ\noned the five external truths — the\n ou\ntermost cov\nerings of divine\n doctrine\n — which are the derived powers of Divine\n Truth in\n its first proceeding.\n\n**\n¶15:** And at the time when\n evil produced\n from\n its works,\n through its further\n offspring, these\n fell upon the natural mind and\n drew strength from the fundamental states of\n fals\nity and were nourished by them\n —\n wickedness together with cruelty gathering\n into the ruling self-love, the\n chief of all evil affections. He\n subd\nued his own\n real\nms and his\n own powers;\n he gathered every\n evil affection into himself.\n He prepared himself\n for spiritual combat;\n he set himself to war\n against the land of wisdom,\n and against\n the Divine 